[0,"o","$ npm run demo -- --format markdown\r\n"]
[0.6,"o","# QualityMax MCP demo — all four tools, one run\n\n| # | Tool | What it produced here |\n|:-:|------|------------------------|\n| 1 | `scan_url` | 17 findings across 8 categories, graded, with measurements |\n| 2 | `inspect_page` | 5 interactive elements, 1 form, role/name locators |\n| 3 | `generate_playwright_repro` | `.qmax-mcp/repros/qmax-repro-1785829858522-3cc8e680.spec.ts` |\n| 4 | `run_playwright_test` | expected **failed** on Chromium |\n\n---\n\n# QA Scan — 127.0.0.1:63260\n\n**Grade: 🔴 F  (0 / 100)**   ·   17 issues found   ·   scanned 2026-08-04\n\n`░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░` 0 / 100\n\n| Category | Issues | Worst |\n|----------|--------|:-----:|\n| Console errors | `███░░░░░░░` 1 | 🔴 high |\n| Broken links | `███░░░░░░░` 1 | 🟠 medium |\n| Accessibility | `████████░░` 3 | 🔴 high |\n| Performance | `░░░░░░░░░░` 0 | — |\n| SEO | `███░░░░░░░` 1 | 🟡 low |\n| Security headers | `██████████` 4 | 🟠 medium |\n| Cookies and trackers | `█████░░░░░` 2 | 🟠 medium |\n| Mixed content | `███░░░░░░░` 1 | 🔵 info |\n| Page weight | `██████████` 4 | 🟠 medium |\n\n---\n\n## Measurements\n\n| Metric | Value |\n|--------|-------|\n| Largest Contentful Paint | 20ms |\n| Cumulative Layout Shift | 0.000 |\n| Time to First Byte | 3ms |\n| First Contentful Paint | 20ms |\n| Interaction to Next Paint | not measured — needs real user interaction |\n| Page transfer | 22 kB across 4 requests |\n| Slowest request | 15ms — http://127.0.0.1:63260/ |\n\nWhere the bytes went:\n\n```\nscript      ████████████████  18 kB\ndocument    ██░░░░░░░░░░░░░░   3 kB\nstylesheet  ██░░░░░░░░░░░░░░   2 kB\nimage       ░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  417 B\n```\n\n_Sampled from one cold load on the scanning machine. Treat it as a signal, not as field data from real users._\n\n_INP is not measured: Interaction to Next Paint requires real user interaction, which this scan does not perform._\n\n_LCP is its value once the network went idle; a later element could still become the largest._\n\n---\n\n## 🔴 high · Form control has no accessible label.\nSelector: `input`\n\n**Reproduce:**\n\n1. Open http://127.0.0.1:63260/\n2. Inspect `input`\n3. Note: Form control has no accessible label.\n\n**Fix:** Associate the control with a visible label or aria-label.\n\n---\n\n## 🔴 high · error: Demo checkout calculation failed\n\n**Reproduce:**\n\n1. Open http://127.0.0.1:63260/\n2. Open DevTools → Console\n3. Observe: Demo checkout calculation failed\n\n**Fix:** Fix runtime errors and warnings before relying on generated tests.\n\n---\n\n## 🟠 medium · Image is missing alt text.\nSelector: `img`\n\n**Reproduce:**\n\n1. Open http://127.0.0.1:63260/\n2. Inspect `img`\n3. Note: Image is missing alt text.\n\n**Fix:** Add meaningful alt text or alt=\"\" for decorative images.\n\n---\n\n## 🟠 medium · Interactive element has no accessible name.\nSelector: `button`\n\n**Reproduce:**\n\n1. Open http://127.0.0.1:63260/\n2. Inspect `button`\n3. Note: Interactive element has no accessible name.\n\n**Fix:** Add visible text or aria-label.\n\n---\n\n## 🟠 medium · 1 session or authentication cookie is readable from JavaScript.\n\n**Reproduce:**\n\n1. Open http://127.0.0.1:63260/\n2. Open DevTools → Application → Cookies\n3. Compare the flags on the listed cookies\n\n**Fix:** Set HttpOnly on session and authentication cookies so injected script cannot exfiltrate them.\n\n---\n\n## 🟠 medium · Link returned HTTP 404.\n`http://127.0.0.1:63260/missing`\n\n**Fix:** Update, redirect, or remove the broken link.\n\n---\n\n## 🟠 medium · Missing content-security-policy header.\n\n**Reproduce:**\n\n```bash\ncurl -sI http://127.0.0.1:63260/ | grep -i content-security-policy\n```\n\n**Fix:** Add a Content-Security-Policy to reduce script injection risk.\n\n---\n\n## 🟠 medium · Missing strict-transport-security header.\n\n**Reproduce:**\n\n```bash\ncurl -sI http://127.0.0.1:63260/ | grep -i strict-transport-security\n```\n\n**Fix:** Add HSTS on HTTPS sites.\n\n---\n\n## 🟠 medium · Page transfers 22 kB, over the 15 kB budget.\n\n**Reproduce:**\n\n1. Open http://127.0.0.1:63260/\n2. Open DevTools → Network with cache disabled\n3. Reload and read the transferred total\n\n**Fix:** Compress and split the largest resource types listed above before adding more to the page.\n\n---\n\n## 🟠 medium · 2 render-blocking resources in <head>, over the 1 budget.\n\n**Reproduce:**\n\n1. Open http://127.0.0.1:63260/\n2. View source\n3. Count <head> scripts without async/defer and non-print stylesheets\n\n**Fix:** Add async or defer to head scripts, and inline or preload only the CSS needed for first paint.\n\n---\n\n## 🟠 medium · 1 script exceeds 15 kB.\n\n**Reproduce:**\n\n1. Open http://127.0.0.1:63260/\n2. Open DevTools → Network with cache disabled\n3. Reload and read the transferred total\n\n**Fix:** Code-split the bundle and load rarely used routes on demand; large scripts also block the main thread.\n\n---\n\n## 🟠 medium · 1 text resource is served without compression.\n\n**Reproduce:**\n\n1. Open http://127.0.0.1:63260/\n2. Open DevTools → Network\n3. Check the content-encoding response header on the listed resources\n\n**Fix:** Enable Brotli or gzip at the origin or CDN. Text assets typically shrink by 70% or more.\n\n---\n\n## 🟡 low · 1 cookie is missing HttpOnly.\n\n**Reproduce:**\n\n1. Open http://127.0.0.1:63260/\n2. Open DevTools → Application → Cookies\n3. Compare the flags on the listed cookies\n\n**Fix:** Set HttpOnly unless client-side JavaScript genuinely needs to read the cookie.\n\n---\n\n## 🟡 low · Missing x-content-type-options header.\n\n**Reproduce:**\n\n```bash\ncurl -sI http://127.0.0.1:63260/ | grep -i x-content-type-options\n```\n\n**Fix:** Add X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff.\n\n---\n\n## 🟡 low · Missing referrer-policy header.\n\n**Reproduce:**\n\n```bash\ncurl -sI http://127.0.0.1:63260/ | grep -i referrer-policy\n```\n\n**Fix:** Add a Referrer-Policy header.\n\n---\n\n## 🟡 low · Meta description is missing or very short.\n\n**Reproduce:**\n\n```bash\ncurl -s http://127.0.0.1:63260/ | grep -i '<meta name=\"description\"'\n```\n\n**Fix:** Add a <meta name=\"description\"> (50–160 chars).\n\n---\n\n## 🔵 info · Mixed content does not apply: the page itself was served over HTTP.\n\n**Fix:** Serve the page over HTTPS, then rescan to check its subresources.\n\nScreenshot: `/var/folders/nk/63t416311tx1dg1p62835pjr0000gn/T/qmax-mcp/scan-1785829858236-w1sx6acnsgd.png`\n\n---\n\n_Scanned by **qmax-mcp** · `npx -y @qualitymax/qmax-mcp scan <url>` · free, local, no account_\n\n---\n\n## Page structure — `inspect_page`\n\nTitle: **Northwind Coffee — checkout** · 3 headings · 1 form · 5 interactive elements\n\nSuggested locators, preferring role and accessible name:\n\n- `page.getByRole('link', { name: \"Pricing\" })`\n- `page.getByRole('link', { name: \"Release notes\" })`\n- `page.getByRole('textbox', { name: \"you@example.com\" })`\n- `page.getByRole('button', { name: \"Complete checkout\" })`\n\n---\n\n## Repro and executed evidence\n\n- Generated: `.qmax-mcp/repros/qmax-repro-1785829858522-3cc8e680.spec.ts`\n- Executed on Chromium: expected **failed** result\n- Execution digest: `676c42870dafce642e68772604be566906e5259fdd3756d0f1f3dc2e1fde1e89`\n- Approval limit: the demo self-asserted this digest. That is not independently verifiable human approval.\n\n---\n\n## What this run does not show\n\n- The fixture is served over HTTP on loopback, so the mixed_content check correctly reports itself as not applicable and no third-party trackers or cookies can appear.\n- Core Web Vitals are measured against a local fixture on this machine, so they are fast by construction and are shown as measurements rather than as a passing grade.\n- The weight budget is deliberately set below the fixture size to demonstrate the check. It is not a recommended budget.\n- The intentionally failing repro proves the scan-to-repro path. It does not resolve QUA-1730’s client-verifiable human-approval requirement.\n"]
